1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
Everyone says time flies when you're

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:02,720
having fun.

3
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,000
That's not quite it.

4
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,760
Monday's meeting lasts a year.

5
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,520
Your weekend lasts ten minutes.

6
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,400
Same clock.

7
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,160
So who's stealing your weekend?

8
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:10,960
Your brain,

9
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,560
and it doesn't even own a clock.

10
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,800
Scientists think it guesses the time by

11
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,480
counting how often you check.

12
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,120
At your desk,

13
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,400
you check constantly,

14
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,000
so the seconds pile up.

15
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:20,960
Here's the catch.

16
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:22,480
On a Saturday you're too busy to

17
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:22,960
look,

18
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,320
so the counting stops.

19
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,520
Fewer counted seconds,

20
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:26,320
less time.

21
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,160
The real clock never slowed.

22
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,560
So time flies when you stop counting.

23
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,160
Fun just helps you forget.

24
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,680
Want a longer weekend?

25
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:34,880
Stare at the clock.

26
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,760
It works great,

27
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,793
and ruins everything.
